[ti:Divinity]
[length:04:32]
[00:08.54]Thirty-nine years... Whis. The dream again. Find me that Saiyan.
[00:39.34]Thirty-nine years asleep; one blink behind my eyes,
[00:41.98]While empires turned to embers in the corners of the skies.
[00:44.62]No cradle, no confession, just the office and the blade;
[00:47.10]I am what the light requires when its monuments decay.
[00:49.58]The Kais may seed the heavens; I decide what cannot stay—
[00:52.14]A garden chokes on everything its keeper fears to slay.
[00:54.70]Yet through my sacred silence came a flash of burning red:
[00:56.94]A stranger crowned in godfire, standing where my dreams lay dead.
[01:00.54]Whis, strike the hour—
[01:02.54]I can taste the coming storm.
[01:04.70]My boredom splits like thunder;
[01:07.50]Something WORTHY takes a form.
[01:10.30]DIVINITY! Hear the pillars BEND!
[01:12.86]HAKAI! I am the mercy of the END!
[01:15.42]One finger, one silence—watch the constellations fall;
[01:17.90]I don't need a throne when I can UNMAKE it all.
[01:20.74]Rise, crimson warrior—make the black sky BRIGHT;
[01:25.10]Prove that something mortal deserves another night!
[01:32.30]One flick—a world forgets the shape its monuments once wore;
[01:35.18]One yawn—the fiercest warlord cannot rise to wage a war.
[01:37.50]Champa snarls across the stars; let my brother count his feasts,
[01:40.14]I want thunder in the silence, not another kneeling beast.
[01:42.70]I can feast upon a thousand worlds, then sleep until they're gone;
[01:45.18]But that phantom pulse keeps pounding like a war-drum before dawn.
[01:47.74]There's a little blue world turning where that crimson fire may breathe;
[01:50.38]Whis, prepare the journey—bring me SOMETHING to believe.
[01:52.70]Let the silence split WIDE OPEN;
[01:55.18]Let the sleeping stars ignite.
[01:57.42]If a mortal wears godfire,
[01:59.90]He can earn the right to FIGHT!
[02:03.02]DIVINITY! Hear the pillars BEND!
[02:05.66]HAKAI! I am the mercy of the END!
[02:08.22]One finger, one silence—watch the constellations fall;
[02:10.70]I don't need a throne when I can UNMAKE it all.
[02:13.42]Rise, crimson warrior—make the black sky BRIGHT;
[02:17.90]Prove that something mortal deserves another night!
[02:54.14]Whis... is that a smile? Don't mock me.
[03:01.58]I haven't felt this awake
[03:04.62]In thirty-nine years.
[03:07.58]A little thread named Shin can bring a god down to his knees;
[03:10.30]Even cosmic kings have chains that no one ever sees.
[03:12.86]And above me, Zeno laughs—such a small and sovereign sound;
[03:15.34]Tell me, what is DIVINITY when every god is bound?
[03:17.90]I was made to clear the garden, not to grieve for every rose;
[03:20.30]Still that crimson ghost inside my dreams refuses to let go.
[03:22.94]If he rises, I will meet him. If he fails, a world may fall—
[03:25.34]But if he makes me HESITATE... perhaps that says it ALL!
[03:28.54]DIVINITY! Hear the pillars BEND!
[03:31.10]HAKAI! I am the mercy of the END!
[03:33.58]One finger, one silence—watch the constellations fall;
[03:36.14]I don't need a throne when I can UNMAKE it all.
[03:38.94]Rise, crimson warrior—make the black sky BRIGHT;
[03:43.26]Prove that something mortal deserves another night!
[03:49.34]The clouds are blue beyond the glass; the stars begin to thin.
[03:54.30]A silent world revolves below, unaware of what's within.
[03:59.10]Whis, slow the journey—let anticipation climb.
[04:03.42]One last breath of silence... then we'll see who's worth my time.
[04:13.50]Now... show me this Super Saiyan God.
